        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0565" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Baker, Charles/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-25T13:00:00-05:00">January 25, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Your 110, January 22, 6 p.m., in reference to capture of Charles Baker.</p>
                <p>Department desires that Legation press this case with the Chinese authorities and
                    that Peck be directed to continue to urge upon the Ministry of Foreign Affairs,
                    as under instruction from the Department, the need for prompt and effective
                    action to effect the release of Baker.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
